 dataset","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"print(train['answer'].isnull().sum())","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### 1.1c Duplication Analysis\n- 242 duplicate prompts means that the same question is present 242 times.\n- Out of those 242 repeated questions, 183 of them are completely the same with the same options and same answers. \n- Remaining 54 repeated questions have different options and are therefore not contradictory.\n- Therefore, the deletion of any rows will have a negative impact.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"n_dup_prompts = train['prompt'].duplicated().sum()\nn_dup_rows = train.duplicated(subset=['prompt'] + OPTIONS).sum()\nprint(f\"Duplicate prompts:     {n_dup_prompts}\")\nprint(f\"Fully-duplicate rows:  {n_dup_rows}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### 1.1d Text Cleaning\n- Intruction prefixes, which carry no informational value and are rather noises can be removed from each prompt\n- Whitespace is normalised\n- Punctuation is maintained as it is ","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"PREFIX = re.compile(\n    r'^(pick the best possible answer|select the most accurate option|'\n    r'identify the correct statement|determine the correct option|'\n    r'choose the correct answer|choose the best answer)[:\\-\\s]*',\n    re.IGNORECASE\n)\n\ndef clean(text):\n    text = PREFIX.sub('', str(text).strip())\n    text = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', text)\n    return text.strip()\n\nfor col in ['prompt'] + OPTIONS:\n    train[col] = train[col].apply(clean)\n\ntrain.head(2)","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Step 2 (TF-IDF) ","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### 1.2a TF-IDF Training Run","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def tfidf_rank(row):\n    \"\"\"Rank the 5 options by TF-IDF cosine similarity to the prompt\"\"\"\n  \n    texts = [row['prompt']] + [row[o] for o in OPTIONS]\n\n    tfidf = TfidfVectorizer().fit_transform(texts)\n\n    sims = cosine_similarity(tfidf[0:1], tfidf[1:]).flatten()\n\n    ranked_idx = sims.argsort()[::-1]       \n    \n    return [OPTIONS[i] for i in ranked_idx][:3]       \n\ntfidf_preds = [tfidf_rank(row) for _, row in train.iterrows()]","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"1.2b Scoring Functions","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def apk(actual, predicted, k=3):\n    \"\"\"Score = 1/rank if the correct answer is in the top-k, else 0.\"\"\"\n    for i, p in enumerate(predicted[:k]):\n        if p == actual:\n            return 1.0 / (i + 1)\n    return 0.0\n\ndef map3(predictions, actuals):\n    \"\"\"Mean Average Precision @3 across all questions.\"\"\"\n    return np.mean([apk(a, p) for p, a in zip(predictions, actuals)])","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### 1.2c TF-IDF Test Run ","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"actuals = train['answer'].tolist()\ntfidf_score = map3(tfidf_preds, actuals)\nprint(f\"TF-IDF MAP@3 on training set: {tfidf_score:.4f}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null}]}